# Normalize to LF in BOTH the repository and the working tree.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true on Windows checks files out as CRLF.
# That is how web/index.html ended up with mixed endings: written as LF by
# one tool, rewritten as CRLF by another, then a cross-line regex silently
# matched nothing (or matched far too much). Pinning the working tree to LF
# makes line endings a property of the repo instead of the machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch is the single exception: cmd.exe still parses CRLF more reliably,
# and start.bat is the one file that must survive a double-click.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Minified vendor blob — never touch its line endings, and keep git from
# spending time diffing it.
web/gsap.min.js -diff text eol=lf